/-!
# Witness data for the finite F-automizer calculation

These tables contain only matrices and words. `Certificate` checks the
exclusion witnesses against the local stabilizer; `FivePoints` checks the
120 distinct representatives and their faithful permutation action.
The five triples in each case are the lines of a spread of the four-dimensional
binary space. They give the five-point action without any classification theorem.

Source: the finite step of Janko, J. Algebra 9 (1968), Section 2, Lemma 2,
pp.4–5. The accompanying `source/Generate.py` generates witness data only;
all mathematical assertions are proved by the Lean kernel.
-/

